// B1 course (A2 → B1 roadmap), module 17 „B1 lugemine ja kirjutamine” (a2b1-081…085), stage B1. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). The module prepares the Harno B1 reading and
// writing parts through real situations, not drills: ads matching (081), a text with multiple choice (081), an option
// cloze (083, 084), a phrase bank with extras (082, 084), a ~50-word message (081, 082, 084) and a ~100-word personal or
// formal letter (082, 084). One storyline: Sofia prepares for her B1 exam in May (module 15's goal) with Maret's course at
// Keelekool Sõna; she reads at home in her Kalamaja wooden house (Valgevase tänav; Tiina is the head of the housing
// association; new neighbour Ruslan), at the course and in the city paper. Goal, said on the first sheet: a mock writing
// part done as real messages — a notice to Sofia's house and a letter to her mother Helgi (084 Kasuta).
//   081 notices and ads — the stairwell and street notices A–F (situations ↔ notices), the local radio news, a city
//       paper article on the house's renovation (multiple choice); Tiina's letter, Sofia explains it to Ruslan.
//   082 letters and messages — Maret's voice message on the writing part, Helgi's letter; Sofia's mail to the school
//       (phrase bank), the exam day questionnaire, the library call; the mock exam clashes with Oskar's 10th birthday —
//       a call to the school's administrator Kaire and a formal e-mail.
//   083 the opinion text — two readers' letters on free language courses (Marina, Peeter); an option cloze, a radio
//       debate (Ülle, Maret, Peeter); classmates' cards (Natalja, Igor, Li), a debate and a reader's letter to the paper.
//   084 the language of data — Tiina's survey on the old laundry room (chart, her talk at the meeting); the school's
//       newsletter on how learners prepare; the final project: the meeting's minutes and Sofia's mock exam results →
//       a ~50-word notice to the house and a ~100-word letter to Helgi.
// No new grammar item (METHODOLOGY_STANDARD §7 places none here); the module spirals the course's B1 grammar inside the
// text types: the impersonal and participles as attributes in notices (081: suletakse, vahetati, suletud tänav; again in
// 084: otsustati, küsitletud), total vs partial object and the quotative in letters (082: sain kirja / ootan vastust,
// olevat vabu kohti), kes / mis relative clauses in the opinion text (083), quantity + partitive and agreement with
// enamik / pooled in data (084). Module 16's words (arvamus, põhjus, eelis, puudus, võrdlema, nõus, vastu, ettepanek,
// kompromiss, kokkulepe, koosolek, hääletama, järeldus, seega …) return throughout. Lesson 5 (085) is the module's check
// in Harno B1 form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b1/module17.js, the v1 file in archive/v1/b1/module17.js.
